1. What this licence covers

"DOOM OS" means the patch, the patcher, and everything they put on an
SP-404MK2: the code, the screens with their layout and design, the pixel
art, icons, typefaces and animations made for it, and its texts. It also
covers the manual and the artwork published with it.

DOOM OS contains no part of Roland's firmware. That firmware belongs to
Roland Corporation and is not covered by this licence. The typefaces of the
manual's web page (Barlow, IBM Plex Mono) keep their own licence, the SIL
Open Font License 1.1.


2. What you may do, free of charge

- Use the patcher to patch firmware you got from Roland, for an SP-404MK2
  you own or use, and keep copies of what it made for your own units.
- Use DOOM OS on that unit for anything, professional and commercial work
  included: playing live, recording, releasing music, teaching. What you
  make with DOOM OS is yours. We claim no right in it.
- Talk about DOOM OS and show it: reviews, videos, screenshots, tutorials
  and posts, with a link to the official release.


3. What you may not do without written permission

- Pass on the patch, the patcher or a patched firmware file, or host them
  anywhere else. Link to the official release instead.
- Change DOOM OS, or copy or closely imitate its code, screens, layouts,
  graphics or texts in anything else: other firmware, patches, apps or
  designs. This holds however the material was obtained, taking DOOM OS
  apart included.
- Sell DOOM OS, rent it out, or charge for it or for access to it.
- Remove or change its copyright notices, or present DOOM OS or any part of
  it as your own work.
- Use the name "DOOM OS" or its logo for anything else.

To ask for permission: lab@klangfeldlabs.com


4. Studying DOOM OS

You may study how DOOM OS works, and what you learn about the SP-404MK2
and its firmware is yours to use, in firmware of your own too. Section 3
protects the work itself: its code, screens, layouts, graphics and texts.
This licence does not take away anything else the law allows you
regardless of it.


